            <ArticleTitle>Synthesis of (+)-Lysergol and Its Analogues To Assess Serotonin Receptor Activity.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>624-627</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1021/acs.orglett.6b03779</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>An efficient synthesis of ergot alkaloid lysergol and its analogues is described, providing compounds for functional evaluation at the human 5-HT1A, 5-HT2A, 5-HT2B, or 5-HT2C receptors. Key features of the synthesis include the development of a tandem reaction to construct the multifunctionalized piperidine skeleton and use of a rhodium-catalyzed [3 + 2] annulation in the late-stage indole formation.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
